 hat in Saturday’s alumni parade.","evidence_claim":"Trinity says the prior 50th reunion class passes the hat at the Half-Century event, and the new class adds a representative pin.","source_url":"https://www.trincoll.edu/abouttrinity/history-traditions/traditions/","source_title":"Traditions | Trinity College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Reunion programming is event-specific; consult current alumni and family event information.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"trinity-owen-morgan-mace","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Owen Morgan Mace","title":"Watch for the Mace in Procession","subtitle":"Academic processions","notes":"During an academic procession, look for the 44-inch Morgan Mace preceding the president and note its six institutional seals.","short_summary":"Presented in 1950, the mace represents the president’s executive authority.","evidence_claim":"Trinity states that the Owen Morgan Mace precedes the president in academic processions and symbolizes executive power.","source_url":"https://www.trincoll.edu/abouttrinity/history-traditions/traditions/","source_title":"Traditions | Trinity College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Visible during applicable College academic ceremonies; timing depends on the current ceremony program.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"trinity-commencement-book","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"The Book","title":"Notice the Book at Commencement","subtitle":"Trinity Commencement","notes":"At Commencement, notice the Book placed in each graduate’s hands, a practice Trinity says began accidentally at its first commencement.","short_summary":"The Book tradition dates to 1827, when President Brownell used the bound order of exercises.","evidence_claim":"Trinity says the Book has been placed in every graduate’s hands since the College’s first commencement in 1827.","source_url":"https://www.trincoll.edu/abouttrinity/history-traditions/traditions/","source_title":"Traditions | Trinity College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Part of Commencement; attendance and viewing arrangements are set by the College for each ceremony.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
